# ============================================================================
# llm-wiki — Environment Variables
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file:  mkdir -p ~/.config/llm-wiki && cp config/.env.example ~/.config/llm-wiki/.env
# Then fill in the values below. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Required vs Optional:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY        — REQUIRED (handled by Claude Code login)
#   MINERU_API_TOKEN         — REQUIRED for PDF ingest (free; cloud backend)
#   LLM_*                    — Optional (enables cross-model review)
# ============================================================================


# --- Anthropic API Key (REQUIRED) -------------------------------------------
# How Claude Code works: it needs an Anthropic API key for LLM calls.
# You do NOT set this here. Instead, run:
#   claude login
# Claude Code will handle authentication automatically.


# --- MinerU API Token (REQUIRED for PDF ingest) -----------------------------
# What it does:  Vision-language PDF parser. tools/prepare_paper_source.py
#                calls MinerU to turn raw PDFs into structured markdown
#                (frontmatter with sections + figures) that /ingest consumes.
# Used by:       /ingest (every PDF), /init (batch PDF preprocessing)
#
# How to get:    1. Go to https://mineru.net/
#                2. Sign up (free)
#                3. Create an API token in account settings
#                4. Copy the token below
#
# Without token: PDF ingest fails. Local-backend escape hatch:
#                  uv pip install -e ".[local]"
#                (downloads several GB of model weights; no token needed)
MINERU_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: override the API base (default is https://mineru.net/api/v4)
# MINERU_API_BASE=https://mineru.net/api/v4


# --- Review LLM (Optional, enables cross-model review) ---------------------
# What it does:  Powers the /review skill and cross-model review in /ideate,
#                /novelty, /exp-eval, /paper-plan, /paper-draft, /rebuttal, etc.
#                Uses a second LLM to independently critique research artifacts.
# Used by:       /review, /novelty, /ideate, /exp-eval, /exp-design,
#                /paper-plan, /paper-draft, /rebuttal, /refine
#
# Works with ANY OpenAI-compatible API. Common providers:
#
#   Provider      | LLM_BASE_URL                                               | Example LLM_MODEL
#   ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | -----------------
#   DeepSeek      | https://api.deepseek.com/v1                                | deepseek-chat
#   OpenAI        | https://api.openai.com/v1                                  | gpt-4o
#   OpenRouter    | https://openrouter.ai/api/v1                               | (any model slug)
#   Qwen          | https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1          | qwen-max
#   SiliconFlow   | https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1                              | (see docs)
#
# How to set up:
#   1. Get an API key from your chosen provider
#   2. Fill in the three variables below
#   3. Restart Claude Code (the MCP server auto-loads these from .env)
#
# Without this:   Skills that use cross-model review skip the review step
#                 and proceed with Claude-only analysis. Everything still works,
#                 but you lose the independent second-opinion benefit.
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_MODEL=
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=    # Optional: fallback model if primary fails
